  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "Here are the steps for easy reproduction of training without losing time trying to discover the combinations of versions of different packages that work and without losing many hours compiling Flash Attention (very annoying!)\n\nThe secret to avoid the compilation is to use a combination that contains pre-compiled binaries (can be checked [here](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/releases), more info [here](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/issues/945#issuecomment-2948520692)). All instructions on this page focus on this\n\n\n## B100 / B200\n\nUse this docker image: `pytorch/pytorch_2.8.0-cuda12.8-cudnn9-devel`\n\nThen login to the instance and run these commands:\n\n```bash\npip install flash_attn\ngit clone https://github.com/sapientinc/HRM\ncd HRM/\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\nThen follow the instructions on README according to the training you plan to do\n\nAdapt the `--nproc-per-node` field to the number of GPUs you are using\n\nThe Sudoku Extreme 1k takes ~1:30h with a single B100\n\n\n## RTX 5090 / 4090 / 3090\n\nIt requires CUDA 12.8 (minimum)\n\nIt does not work with `adam-atan2` package so we use `adam-atan2-pytorch` instead\n\nUse this docker image: `pytorch/pytorch_2.8.0-cuda12.8-cudnn9-devel`\n\nThen login to the instance and run these commands:\n\n```bash\npip install flash_attn\ngit clone https://github.com/sapientinc/HRM\ncd HRM\nsed -i 's/adam-atan2/adam-atan2-pytorch/g' requirements.txt \npip install -r requirements.txt\nsed -i 's/adam_atan2/adam_atan2_pytorch/g' pretrain.py\nsed -i 's/AdamATan2/AdamAtan2/g' pretrain.py\nsed -i 's/lr=0,/lr=0.0001,/g' pretrain.py\n```\n\nThen follow the instructions on README according to the training you plan to do\n\nAdapt the `--nproc-per-node` field to the number of GPUs you are using\n\nThe Sudoku Extreme 1k takes less than 2h with a single 5090\nAnd it can take ~1h 35min if you set the `eval_interval` to the same value as `epochs` (default is 20000)",
